From: dArkOS RG52 Mini port
Subject: OpenGL keeps the GPU work on the emulation thread

azahar-nano's async GPU worker (mode 3 by default on Mali) runs the
rasterizer on its own thread. Vulkan can be driven from any thread; an OpenGL
context, RetroArch's gl driver here, is current on the frontend's thread only.
With citra_graphics_api OpenGL every game crashed at its first draw: the GL
rasterizer called from the worker had no context, a mapping came back null
and SyncAndUploadLUTs wrote through it (SIGSEGV at address 0, tid of the
worker). AsyncModeFromProps() returns 0 for OpenGL.

